

TODO: Implement Custom Compression for Blueprint Instances

Objective:
Design a compression system optimized for Minecraft worlds and server data to reduce storage and transfer size while maintaining fast access.

Proposed Approach (PAC Algorithm):

1. Chunk Aggregation:
   - Uncompress all chunks of a Minecraft world.
   - Merge the chunk data into a single contiguous file to reduce per-chunk overhead.

2. Delta Compression
   - For worlds derived from a common base:
     - Divide the aggregated file into fixed-size data blocks.
     - Compare each block against the base file.
     - Store only the blocks that have changed, along with their offsets.
     - This approach can drastically reduce storage when most of the data is unchanged.

3. Compression Layer:
   - Compress the aggregated file (and any server metadata) using a high-performance algorithm such as LZ4 or Zstd.